    "doc": "E-026 arm: TWO RINGS of eight \u2014 stencil:17 ring:222-555, seed 0. Chris's spec: 'two rings, eight points each.' Centre + 8 points at 222 km + 8 at 555 km, the outer ring rotated half a sector off the inner so the shape samples 16 bearings rather than 8 twice. Paired against e023r222 (ONE ring of 8 at 222 km, same recipe and seeds, corridor AUC 0.6043) and e017 (no neighbours, 0.5837) -- both already trained and already rolled by the same evaluator behind the same gate. This is the width/reach question moved out of the ridge, which Chris rightly distrusts: the ridge scored this exact shape at +0.0087 against the single ring's +0.0123, i.e. WORSE for double the width, while E-022 says the real model pays for width and E-023 says a second scale is where the information is. Falsifier: corridor AUC above ~0.619 means the second ring earns its width. Entry: ml/EXPERIMENTS.md E-026.",
